n\"},{\"word\":\"parāyaṇaḥ\",\"translation\":\"being so destined\"},{\"word\":\"vigata\",\"translation\":\"having discarded\"},{\"word\":\"icchā\",\"translation\":\"wishes\"},{\"word\":\"bhaya\",\"translation\":\"fear\"},{\"word\":\"krodhaḥ\",\"translation\":\"anger\"},{\"word\":\"yaḥ\",\"translation\":\"one who\"},{\"word\":\"sadā\",\"translation\":\"always\"},{\"word\":\"muktaḥ\",\"translation\":\"liberated\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"saḥ\",\"translation\":\"he is\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":1740,\"bb\":1538,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/27-28/b1538/\",\"body_value\":\"Shutting out all external sense objects, keeping the eyes and vision concentrated between the two eyebrows, suspending the inward and outward breaths within the nostrils, and thus controlling the mind, senses and intelligence, the transcendentalist aiming at liberation becomes free from desire, fear and anger. One who is always in this state is certainly liberated.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1741,\"bb\":1539,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/27-28/b1539/\",\"body_value\":\"Being engaged in Kṛṣṇa consciousness, one can immediately understand one’s spiritual identity, and then one can understand the Supreme Lord by means of devotional service. When one is well situated in devotional service, one comes to the transcendental position, qualified to feel the presence of the Lord in the sphere of one’s activity. This particular position is called liberation in the Supreme.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1742,\"bb\":1540,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/27-28/b1540/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1743,\"bb\":1541,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/27-28/b1541/\",\"body_value\":\"This yoga process helps one become free from all kinds of fear and anger and thus feel the presence of the Supersoul in the transcendental situation. In other words, Kṛṣṇa consciousness is the easiest process of executing yoga principles. This will be thoroughly explained in the next chapter. A Kṛṣṇa conscious person, however, being always engaged in devotional service, does not risk losing his senses to some other engagement. This is a better way of controlling the senses than by aṣṭāṅga-yoga.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 5.27-28\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 5.27-28\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-4 w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-auto md:px-8 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"className\":\"breadcrumb mb-8 text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"children\":\"Library\"}],\" » \"]}],[\"$\",