nced_view\":true,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]},\"next\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/2/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 2\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":1754,\"bb\":568108,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/1/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"श्रीभगवानुवाच
अनाश्रित: कर्मफलं कार्यं कर्म करोति य: ।
स सन्न्यासी च योगी च न निरग्न‍िर्न चाक्रिय: ॥ १ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":1755,\"bb\":1553,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/1/b1553/\",\"body_value\":\"śrī-bhagavān uvāca
anāśritaḥ karma-phalaṁ
kāryaṁ karma karoti yaḥ
sa sannyāsī ca yogī ca
na niragnir na cākriyaḥ\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":1756,\"bb\":1554,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/1/b1554/\",\"shadow_value\":\"śrī-bhagavān uvāca – the Lord said; anāśritaḥ – without taking shelter; karma-phalam – of the result of work; kāryam – obligatory; karma – work; karoti – performs; yaḥ – one who; saḥ – he; sannyāsī – in the renounced order; ca – also; yogī – mystic; ca – also; na – not; niḥ – without; agniḥ – fire; na – nor; ca – also; akriyaḥ – without duty.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"śrī-bhagavān uvāca\",\"translation\":\"the Lord said\"},{\"word\":\"anāśritaḥ\",\"translation\":\"without taking shelter\"},{\"word\":\"karma-phalam\",\"translation\":\"of the result of work\"},{\"word\":\"kāryam\",\"translation\":\"obligatory\"},{\"word\":\"karma\",\"translation\":\"work\"},{\"word\":\"karoti\",\"translation\":\"performs\"},{\"word\":\"yaḥ\",\"translation\":\"one who\"},{\"word\":\"saḥ\",\"translation\":\"he\"},{\"word\":\"sannyāsī\",\"translation\":\"in the renounced order\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"yogī\",\"translation\":\"mystic\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"not\"},{\"word\":\"niḥ\",\"translation\":\"without\"},{\"word\":\"agniḥ\",\"translation\":\"fire\"},{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"nor\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"akriyaḥ\",\"translation\":\"without duty\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":1757,\"bb\":1555,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/1/b1555/\",\"body_value\":\"The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: One who is unattached to the fruits of his work and who works as he is obligated is in the renounced order of life, and he is the true mystic, not he who lights no fire and performs no duty.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1758,\"bb\":1556,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/1/b1556/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1759,\"bb\":1557,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/1/b1557/\",\"body_value\":\"The sannyāsīs sometimes artificially think that they have become liberated from all material duties, and therefore they cease to perform agnihotra yajñas (fire sacrifices), but actually they are self-interested because their goal is to become one with the impersonal Brahman. Such a desire is greater than any material desire, but it is not without self-interest. Similarly, the mystic yogī who practices the yoga system with half-open eyes, ceasing all material activities, desires some satisfaction for his personal self. But a person acting in Kṛṣṇa consciousness works for the satisfaction of the whole, without self-interest. A Kṛṣṇa conscious person has no desire for self-satisfaction. His criterion of success is the satisfaction of Kṛṣṇa, and thus he is the perfect sannyāsī, or perfect yogī. Lord Caitanya, the highest perfectional symbol of renunciation, prays in this way:\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":1760,\"bb\":1558,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/1/b1558/\",\"body_value\":\"na dhanaṁ na janaṁ na sundarīṁ
kavitāṁ vā jagad-īśa kāmaye
mama janmani janmanīśvare
bhavatād bhaktir ahaitukī tvayi\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1761,\"bb\":1559,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/1/b1559/\",\"body_value\":\"“O Almighty Lord, I have no desire to accumulate wealth, nor to enjoy beautiful women. Nor do I want any number of followers. What I want only is the causeless mercy of Your devotional service in my life, birth after birth.”\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 6.1\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 6.1\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-4 w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-auto md:px-8 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"className\":\"breadcrumb mb-8 text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"children\":\"Library\"}],\" » \"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/bg/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/bg/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-lin